{
  "requirement": "The `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: false.** The behavior is correct, but the `{impl}` marking is incomplete and the requirement has no `{test}` reference.\n\n**What the requirement says.** `requirements.cli.clap` (md/requirements/cli.md) says the CLI \"MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.\"\n\n**Behavior is satisfied.**\n- `Cargo.toml` depends on `clap` 4.6.7 with the `derive` feature.\n- `src/main.rs` imports `clap::{ArgGroup, Parser, Subcommand}`.\n- `struct Cli` derives `Parser`, and `main` calls `Cli::parse()`. Both carry `{impl}` markers for this requirement (lines 10 and 89).\n- A search of the sources found no manual argument parsing such as `std::env::args`.\n- The commands and options are declared with clap derive attributes: `#[arg]`, `ArgGroup`, `conflicts_with`, `alias`, `hide`, and the subcommand enums.\n\n**Gap 1: the definitions are not marked `{impl}`.**\n- The requirement says clap must be used to *define* commands and options.\n- That definition lives in `enum Command` (src/main.rs lines 18–76), `enum MdbookCommand` (78–81) and `enum HookCommand` (83–86).\n- None of these carries `{impl}`/`{cite}` for `requirements.cli.clap`. `references` lists only `struct[Cli]` and `fn[main]` as implementing sites.\n- So the code that does most of the defining is not marked as implementing the requirement.\n\n**Gap 2: no test is linked to the requirement.**\n- `references` shows no `{test}` site for `requirements.cli.clap`.\n- Related tests exist but are cited for other requirements. `tests/cli.rs` checks `Usage: habeas` for unknown commands and bad options and is cited for `requirements.cli.invocation`. `tests/commands.rs` checks `--help` output and is cited for `status` and `info`.\n- These tests exercise clap-generated behavior. They are not linked to this requirement, and nothing records why a structural requirement like this would not need its own test.\n\n**Acknowledged gaps.** None. There is no FIXME in the source or tests for this subject.\n\nTo fix this, add `{impl}`/`{cite}` markers to the command enums, and add a `{test}` link, for example from the existing usage and help tests.",
